From: Arena Agent Mode
Subject: [PATCH] ci: enforce ruff, a coverage floor, and packaging in CI

The Arena GitHub App is not permitted to push .github/workflows changes,
so this patch is provided separately. Apply it with:

    git apply ci-improvements.patch

It adds three jobs:

  lint       ruff has been configured in pyproject.toml for a long time but
             was never actually run anywhere. It passes clean today; this
             keeps it that way.

  coverage   A floor (--fail-under=55), not a target, measured against
             production code only. Raise it whenever the real number
             comfortably clears it so coverage can only ratchet upwards.

  packaging  Builds a wheel, installs it, and runs the console script from
             OUTSIDE the source tree, asserting the wheel version matches
             organize.VERSION. This is the job that would have caught the
             broken `organize = "organize:main"` entry point, which every
             other job missed because they all invoke `python organize.py`
             by path.

It also updates the byte-compile step for the 10bit.py -> bitdepth.py rename.
---
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -40,7 +40,7 @@
       - name: Byte-compile every script (syntax gate)
         run: >-
           python -m compileall -q
-          organize.py pipeline.py jellyfin_one_shot.py 10bit.py
+          organize.py pipeline.py jellyfin_one_shot.py bitdepth.py
           library_auditor.py mkv_track_cleaner.py movie_standardizer.py
           subtitle_fetcher.py sync_subtitles.py
 
@@ -50,6 +50,78 @@
       - name: Unit test suite (fully offline)
         run: python -m unittest discover -s tests -p "test_*.py"
 
+  lint:
+    # ruff has been configured in pyproject.toml for a long time but was never
+    # actually run anywhere. It passes clean today; this keeps it that way.
+    name: Lint (ruff)
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    steps:
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5
+        with:
+          python-version: "3.11"
+      - run: pip install ruff
+      - name: ruff check
+        run: ruff check --output-format=github .
+
+  coverage:
+    # A floor, not a target. Raise `--fail-under` whenever the real number
+    # comfortably clears it so coverage can only ratchet upwards.
+    name: Coverage gate
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    steps:
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5
+        with:
+          python-version: "3.11"
+      - run: pip install coverage
+      - name: Run suite under coverage
+        run: python -m coverage run -m unittest discover -s tests -p "test_*.py"
+      - name: Report and enforce the floor
+        run: |
+          python -m coverage report
+          python -m coverage report --fail-under=55
+
+  packaging:
+    # Regression guard for the broken console entry point: pyproject declared
+    # `organize = "organize:main"` with no build backend and no package, so the
+    # install succeeded and the command then died with ModuleNotFoundError.
+    # Every other job runs `python organize.py` by path and cannot see that.
+    name: Packaging (install + console script)
+    runs-on: ${{ matrix.os }}
+    strategy:
+      fail-fast: false
+      matrix:
+        os: [ubuntu-latest, windows-latest]
+    steps:
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5
+        with:
+          python-version: "3.11"
+      - name: Build a wheel and install it
+        run: |
+          pip install build
+          python -m build --wheel
+          pip install dist/*.whl
+        shell: bash
+      - name: The console script must work from OUTSIDE the source tree
+        working-directory: ${{ runner.temp }}
+        run: |
+          organize --version
+          organize doctor
+          organize audit --help
+        shell: bash
+      - name: The wheel's version must match organize.VERSION
+        working-directory: ${{ runner.temp }}
+        run: |
+          python -c "
+          import importlib.metadata as m, organize, sys
+          wheel, src = m.version('organize'), organize.VERSION
+          print(f'wheel={wheel} source={src}')
+          sys.exit(0 if wheel == src else 1)
+          "
+        shell: bash
+
   doctor-smoke:
     # Verifies the unified CLI boots and the diagnostic doctor runs green-box
     # on a pristine machine (no binaries, no API key — warnings, not crashes).
